# Round 18, C2-1 (fixed). L §5.10 The sign rule: "3. at the close, after the readings at the day's end"; E §4.2 step 5:
# "then, in step 4, the closing readings together". a and b open at 100.00 PLN and pad from the claim y (min 0, at 0):
# a's closing reading 130.00 pads 30.00 PLN out of y, b's 70.00 pads 30.00 PLN into it, which leave y at 0.00 PLN
# together: no refusal (snap11 tested the pads one by one, refused a's, and then broke conservation, ENGINE-INVARIANT).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
source bk "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place a: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place b: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place y: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

ask q: bal(y, 2026-03-31), bal(a, 2026-03-31), bal(b, 2026-03-31)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[a] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[b] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[y] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version st
  cite bk
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  pad a from y
  pad b from y
  stated[a] = 130.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
  stated[b] = 70.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
=== expect
q: (0.00 PLN, 130.00 PLN, 70.00 PLN)
  pad: a 2026-03-31 end, pads:st:a@2026-03-31 end of 30.00 PLN
  pad: b 2026-03-31 end, pads:st:b@2026-03-31 end of -30.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-30
